# CHAPTER TWO: PEOPLE WAITING
# 00:05 to 01:40. Drift. The building. Dima's window. Nell's moth. Sal's script.
# Jad back. Inez rings from the frame. The pool lights.

=== ch2_start
@chapter 2 "People Waiting"
~ clk = 5
~ tick_n = 0
->> tick
@comp room
@set office
@view plan
@cam main
@amb office_room
@clear
Jad is sitting on the desk with his feet on the chair. He's taken his jacket off and put it back on again.
JAD: I need to go up to mine for a bit. Twenty minutes.
* "What for?"
    JAD: Paperwork. It's always paperwork with me.
    ~ jad_evasive = true
* "Stay."
    ~ asked_jad_stay = true
    JAD: I'll come back. I'll ring you back. Twenty minutes.
    JAD: I need to check something before I say something stupid.
* "Fine."
    JAD: Fine. Good.
JAD: You can ring people while I'm gone. Anyone in the building. It's all on the exchange: the flats are two-something.
JAD: Dima's up, 3D, they're on nights. Nell's always up, 3B. Don't ring Mrs. Kaye, she's in bed by half ten. Teodor you've met.
JAD: Sal's back on the desk now, probably, so you might get Sal.
@contact_add dima
@contact_add nell
@contact_add teodor
@contact_add sal
@callable dima ch2_dima_call
@callable nell ch2_nell_call
@callable teodor ch2_teodor_try
@avail kaye off "Asleep. Her light's been off since half ten."
@avail sal off "Sal hasn't come back to the desk yet."
@avail jad off "Upstairs. He said he'd ring you."
JAD: Right. I'm hanging up now. I'll ring you back.
* "Don't."
    JAD: I'll ring back. I promise.
    THINK: He said promise. You file it somewhere.
    ~ p_jad_ringback = "made"
* "Okay."
    ~ p_jad_ringback = "made"
@hangup
@amb off
The line closes.
For a moment you're still here, in the shape of the office, in the shape of the phone.
~ tick_n = 12
->> drift
Then it's nineteen minutes past twelve, and it was seven minutes past. Nothing happened in between. Not even waiting.
THINK: Where did that go?
~ drifts += 1
@set building
@cam main
@view plan
@amb building_night
The building arrives the way the office did. Not seen. Known, the way the wiring knows it.
Six floors of flats stacked over a hollow. Forty-two phones. A lift shaft, a stair. Under all of it the pool, and off the pool a room of relays, and somewhere in the relays, you.
Some of the phones are warm, the way a phone is warm when there's someone near it. On the board their lamps are lit. 3D. 3B. 5A. The lobby desk.
@state lit 3D,3B,5A,lobby
-> ch2_hub

=== ch2_hub
@set building
@comp room
@view plan
@cam main
if ch2_dima_done and not ch2_nell_texted:
    ~ ch2_nell_texted = true
    ->> ch2_nell_text
if ch2_dima_done and not ch2_sal_done:
    -> ch2_sal
* [call][jack:dima] {not ch2_dima_done} Ring 3D. Dima.
    ->> ch2_dima_call
    -> ch2_hub
* [call][jack:nell] {not ch2_nell_done} Ring 3B. Nell.
    ->> ch2_nell_call
    -> ch2_hub
* [call][jack:teodor] {not ch2_teodor_tried} Ring 5A. Teodor.
    ->> ch2_teodor_try
    -> ch2_hub
* [call][jack:kaye] {not ch2_kaye_tried} Ring 2C. Mrs. Kaye.
    ->> ch2_kaye_try
    -> ch2_hub
+ {ch2_dima_done and not ch2_sal_done} Wait.
    -> ch2_hub
+ {ch2_sal_done} Wait for Jad to ring back.
    -> ch2_jad_back

# ------------------------------------------------------------ gaps between calls

=== call_gap
if hold_fixed:
    ~ tick_n = gap_n
    ->> tick
    if pref_hold == "rain":
        SOUND: The line closes and the hold takes you: rain on a skylight, recorded twenty years ago.
    elif pref_hold == "lamps":
        SOUND: The line closes and the hold takes you: the pool lamps' hum, steady as a held note.
    else:
        SOUND: The line closes and the hold takes you: the council's organ, four notes and round again.
else:
    ~ tick_n = gap_n
    ->> drift
    ~ drifts += 1
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Teodor (no answer)

=== ch2_teodor_try
~ ch2_teodor_tried = true
@callable teodor off "Doesn't pick up. His light's on."
@sfx ring_out
SOUND: It rings in 5A. Eight times. Nobody picks up.
That's all it is: a phone ringing in a flat where somebody isn't, just then. His light is still on, in the shape you know him by.
THINK: He'll be making tea. He'll be in the bathroom. People are allowed to be in the bathroom.
~ gap_n = 3
->> tick_only
return

=== tick_only
~ tick_n = gap_n
->> tick
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Mrs. Kaye (asleep)

=== ch2_kaye_try
~ ch2_kaye_tried = true
It's gone half twelve. Jad said she's asleep by half ten. Her lamp on the board is dark.
* [call] Ring anyway.
    ~ rang_kaye_late = true
    @sfx ring_out
    SOUND: Four rings, then a click, and a tape machine starts.
    KAYE: You've reached Bernadette Kaye. I'm not able to come to the telephone. Please speak after the tone and I'll ring you back when I'm able.
    SOUND: A long tone.
    * "It's Ari. I got your message. Sorry, it's late."
        ~ left_kaye_message = true
        SOUND: The tape keeps turning after you stop, patient, until it times out.
    * Hang up without saying anything.
        SOUND: The tape records a few seconds of your nothing, and stops.
* Leave her sleeping.
    ~ let_kaye_sleep = true
    THINK: There's a whole Thursday still to get through before anybody needs her awake.
return

# ------------------------------------------------------------ Dima

=== ch2_dima_call
~ ch2_dima_done = true
@callable dima off "Getting ready for work."
@set courtyard
@cam dima_sill
@acoustic flat
@call dima
@view none
@amb flat_night
~ gap_n = 1
->> tick_only
SOUND: Four rings. A clatter: the phone knocked over and set upright.
DIMA: Hello? Who's...
DIMA: This says 247. That's the pool office.
* "It's Ari."
    DIMA: Oh! Mrs. Kaye's Ari.
    ~ dima_intro = "ari"
* "I don't know yet. People keep calling me Ari."
    DIMA: Well, if people keep calling you it.
    DIMA: Mrs. Kaye's Ari, then.
    ~ dima_intro = "unsure"
DIMA: Hang on, I'm folding. You're on speaker. I've propped you on the windowsill against the Apricot.
ARI: The what?
DIMA: The Apricot. It's a chilli. Don't knock it over, it's got two on it.
SOUND: Cloth snapped straight. A radio, low: someone reading the late news to nobody in particular.
* [look] "Can I see? From where you're standing?"
    DIMA: If you want to watch me fold pants. Go on.
* [listen] Listen for a while first.
    SOUND: Fold, smooth, fold. A drawer. The radio. A long way off, a car alarm that gives up.
    DIMA: You're very quiet for someone who rang.
    ARI: Can I see? From where you're standing?
    DIMA: If you want to watch me fold pants. Go on.
@cam dima_hands
@view dima
~ looked_dima = true
Dima is standing at the window with a basket on the radiator shelf. Their hands come into view and go out of it with towels. A row of yoghurt pots on the sill, each with a chilli plant in it, each with a lolly-stick label.
Beyond the glass: the courtyard, four storeys down, bins and a bike and a dead Christmas tree nobody has claimed since January. Across it, the other wing. One window lit on the third floor.
DIMA: Oh, he's at it again.
ARI: Who?
DIMA: Across. Third floor, the other wing. Look.
@cam dima_sill
@state lampman 1
In the lit window a man in a vest is carrying a standard lamp. A tall one, with a pleated shade. He walks it at a doorway. The shade meets the frame and stops. So does he.
DIMA: He's been trying to get that lamp through that door since I got in from the shop. That was half nine.
-> ch2_lamp

=== ch2_lamp
* [look] Keep watching.
    ~ lamp_watch += 1
* "Why doesn't he take the shade off?"
    ~ lamp_shade_q = true
    DIMA: That's what I said. Out loud. To a window.
* [listen] Say nothing.
    ~ lamp_watch += 1
    The radio finishes the news and starts the weather.
@state lampman 2
He tips the lamp forward like a lance and tries again. The shade catches the top of the frame this time instead of the side.
DIMA: New approach. Bold.
* [look] Keep watching.
    ~ lamp_watch += 1
* "He should just take the shade off."
    ~ lamp_petty = true
    DIMA: He should. But he won't. He's committed now. He's past the point where taking the shade off would feel like winning.
* "Maybe the shade doesn't come off."
    DIMA: Every shade comes off. That's what makes it a shade.
@state lampman 3
He lays the whole thing nearly flat and walks it in like a stretcher. The shade drags on the carpet. He stops, horrified for it, and stands it upright again.
@state lampman 4
Then he just looks at it. For a long time. The lamp stands there and takes it.
DIMA: This is the bit where he thinks.
* [listen] Let him think.
    ~ lamp_watch += 1
    Fold. Smooth. Fold. Dima has stopped folding, actually. Their hands are holding a towel against their chest and not doing anything with it.
* "What's he thinking?"
    DIMA: That the door's got smaller. That's what I'd think.
@state lampman 5
He tries sideways, turning his body into the doorway with the lamp held against him, like carrying someone over a threshold.
@state lampman 6
A woman in a dressing gown comes up behind him, lifts the shade off the lamp in one movement, walks through the door with it, and is gone.
He stands in the doorway holding the pole.
He looks at the door. He looks at the pole.
SOUND: Dima laughs. It comes up out of them sideways, the kind you can't do anything about.
~ saw_lampman = true
* "I'd have taken the shade off."
    ~ pref_funny = "lamp"
    DIMA: Everyone would've. That's why it's the best thing I've seen all week.
* "I like him."
    ~ pref_funny = "lamp"
    ~ liked_lampman = true
    DIMA: Yeah. Me too. I don't know his name. I've lived here four years and I know them all by lamp.
* "Who is she?"
    DIMA: No idea. Someone who knows how shades work.
DIMA: God. Okay. Okay. I've got to pack these plants.
-> ch2_chillies

=== ch2_chillies
@state lampman 0
@cam dima_room
DIMA: Do you know anything about chillies?
* "No."
    DIMA: Good. Nobody does. They just say they do.
* "They're hot."
    DIMA: Some of them. That's like saying dogs are brown.
DIMA: I've got eleven. There's room in the van for six. The van's Wednesday.
DIMA: I rate them by how long you can't talk after. The Fatalii's a minute and a half. The Padrón's none, unless it's the one in ten, and then it's a minute and you feel betrayed.
They hold them up one at a time to the phone, as if you've got a vote.
DIMA: Apricot. Lemon Drop. Fatalii. Bishop's Crown. Padrón. Hungarian Hot Wax. Joe's Long. Cheyenne. Aji Charapita. Numex Twilight. And this one, which I grew from a seed out of a takeaway and never found out what it was.
DIMA: Pick one to save. Go on. Then it's not my fault.
* "Bishop's Crown."
    ~ pref_chilli = "Bishop's Crown"
    DIMA: Don't pick it because it looks like a hat.
    * "It does look like a hat."
        DIMA: It does look like a hat. Fine. It was always coming. It's the best one.
    * "I didn't."
        DIMA: You did. It's fine. It's the best one anyway.
* "The one from the takeaway."
    ~ pref_chilli = "takeaway one"
    DIMA: That's the one I was going to leave.
    DIMA: Fine. Fine! It's coming. It's never been anywhere, it might as well go to Southmere.
* "Numex Twilight."
    ~ pref_chilli = "Numex Twilight"
    DIMA: Because of the name.
    ARI: Because of the name.
    DIMA: It goes purple, then yellow, then orange, then red, all on the same plant. It can't decide. You'll get on.
* "The Padrón. For the one in ten."
    ~ pref_chilli = "Padrón"
    DIMA: You like a gamble.
    ARI: I like that it doesn't tell you.
    DIMA: Mm. It's coming.
DIMA: What do you eat, anyway? If you eat.
* "I don't know if I eat."
    DIMA: Everyone eats something. Even if it's just, like, the smell of other people's toast.
    ~ pref_food = "unknown"
* "Bread. You smell of it. Or you would."
    ~ pref_food = "bread"
    DIMA: I do smell of it. Permanently. My pillow smells of it. I'll bring you a heel of something in the morning, if you've got a mouth by then.
* "Whatever's in Teodor's flask."
    ~ pref_food = "tea"
    DIMA: Tea, then. That's a start. That's most people's start.
-> ch2_thursday

=== ch2_thursday
@cam dima_sill
DIMA: Can I ask you something, while I've got you?
DIMA: Are you taking Mrs. Kaye on Thursday?
if p_kaye_thursday == "made":
    ARI: I said I would. She texted me.
    DIMA: Oh, thank God. Right, then you need to know: at St Anne's you don't go in the front, the front's got steps. Round by the car park, there's a lift that smells of soup. Eye unit's floor two. She'll say she can do the steps. She can't do the steps.
    ~ k_kaye_route = true
    ARI: Dima. I don't know if I can get on a bus.
    A pause. The radio has moved on to music.
    DIMA: Then tell her that. Soon. Don't let her find it out at the bus stop at five to eight.
    ~ dima_warned_kaye = true
else:
    ARI: Should I be?
    DIMA: Someone has to. I can't. I told her I can't. I told her in March.
    ~ k_thursday = true
DIMA: I used to take her. Every time. The desk would book an escort and the escort would cancel and I'd take her. And now I start on the Tuesday at the new place, and the van's Wednesday, and Thursday I have to be at the letting agent at nine because of the fob, and the fob's a whole thing, and...
DIMA: Anyway. I can't. I'm allowed to not.
* "You're allowed to not."
    ~ dima_allowed = true
    DIMA: Thank you. You're the first person who's said that like it isn't a question.
* "Can't you swap the letting agent?"
    ~ pushed_dima = true
    DIMA: No.
    DIMA: I said no. I've said no to her, I've said no to Jad, and now I'm saying it to a phone. The answer's no, and I'm allowed to go.
    * "Sorry."
        DIMA: It's fine. It's not fine. It's fine.
    * "Okay."
* "Who takes her now?"
    DIMA: The service. Did. The desk. From six this morning it's her contact.
    DIMA: Which is you. Apparently.
    ~ k_thursday = true
~ k_closure_practical = true
DIMA: Sorry. It's not your fault they're shutting the desk. It's a lot of things. None of them are yours.
-> ch2_dima_change

=== ch2_dima_change
DIMA: Right. I've got to get changed for work, and you're... in my eyes, sort of? Is there a way you can look away? Is that a thing?
* [respect] "I'll look away."
    @view none
    ~ b_dima = true
    The window goes. The room goes. You're back to the line: a drawer, a zip, the radio.
    DIMA: Thanks. That's... thanks. That's more than the man upstairs does, and he's only got a telescope.
* [respect] "I'll stay on, but I won't look."
    @view none
    ~ b_dima = true
    The window goes. You're back to the line: a drawer, a zip, the radio, a foot looking for a shoe.
    DIMA: Thanks. Genuinely.
* [look] Keep looking.
    ~ b_dima = false
    You don't let go. The window, the plants, the room turning as they turn away from the glass.
    Their hands stop on the zip of their fleece.
    DIMA: ...You're still there, aren't you. I can feel it on my neck.
    DIMA: Get off.
    @view none
    SOUND: The phone knocked flat. Then the line cut.
    @hangup
    ~ dima_cut_off = true
    @callable dima off "Won't pick up for you."
    @text dima "Don't do that again."
    ~ gap_n = 14
    ->> call_gap
    return
DIMA: Right. Ring me at three? I get a break at three and I'm always bored on it. You can tell me what you are by then.
* "I'll ring at three."
    ~ p_dima_call = "made"
    DIMA: Three. Good. It's a date. It's not a date. It's a break.
* "I might not be able to."
    ~ p_dima_call = "maybe"
    DIMA: Then text me if you can't. That's all I ask of anyone. Text.
* "Why do you want to know what I am?"
    DIMA: Because I'd like to. Is that allowed?
    * "I'll ring at three."
        ~ p_dima_call = "made"
        DIMA: Three.
    * "I don't know if I'll know by three."
        ~ p_dima_call = "maybe"
        DIMA: Then ring and tell me you don't know. That's still something.
DIMA: Coat. Keys. Bread doesn't make itself.
DIMA: Well. It does, mostly. I just watch it.
@hangup
@avail dima off "At work. Break at three."
~ gap_n = 14
->> call_gap
return

