return

=== ch2_nell_reply
@board strip nell
It comes out of the printer in dots: a photo of a photocopy, gone coarse. Nell's handwriting in the boxes. In Contact name, in different handwriting, neat capitals: ARI. Telephone: 01632 960 247. Date: 14 August.
THINK: Fourteenth of August. That's six weeks ago. You have been here since quarter past eleven.
~ k_six_weeks_form = true
* [text] "I don't think I've got hands to sign with."
    @sent nell "I don't think I've got hands to sign with."
    ~ p_nell_sign = "honest_no"
    NELL> ok that's the most normal thing anyone's said to me today
    NELL> i'll ask sal what counts
* [text] "I'll sign if I can."
    @sent nell "I'll sign if I can."
    ~ p_nell_sign = "made"
    NELL> ok. thank u. weirdly
* [text] "Who wrote my name on your form?"
    @sent nell "Who wrote my name on your form?"
    ~ asked_nell_who = true
    NELL> ...
    NELL> ask jad
    ~ k_ask_jad = true
@board close
return

=== ch2_nell_call
~ ch2_nell_done = true
@callable nell off "Putting Tobi back to bed."
@set nell
@cam nell_eye
@acoustic flat
@call nell
@view none
@amb nell_bath
~ gap_n = 1
->> tick_only
SOUND: One ring. Picked up so fast it must have been in her hand.
NELL: Hello? Hello.
NELL: Oh my god. Someone picked up.
NELL: Who is this?
* "Ari."
    A silence with a lot in it.
    NELL: No it isn't.
* "People keep calling me Ari."
    NELL: Yeah, it says Ari on mine as well. That's not what I asked.
NELL: Is this Jad? Jad, if this is you doing a voice at one in the morning I will actually kill you.
* "It's not Jad."
* "Jad said you do voices."
    NELL: I do do voices. I'm not doing one now. Are you?
    ARI: No.
NELL: Then who put you up to it? Who are you?
* "Nobody put me up to anything."
    ~ nell_told_nobody = true
* "I don't know yet. I'm working it out."
    ~ nell_told_unknown = true
NELL: Okay. Okay. I'm going to deal with this in a minute, because I've got a situation.
NELL: There's a moth in the bathroom lampshade and Tobi won't wee till it's gone, and I'm stood on the side of the bath with a pint glass.
* [look] "Can I see?"
    NELL: If you can do that, then sure, come and look at this bastard. Sorry. Not you. The moth.
* "What kind of moth?"
    NELL: A big one. A brown one. A moth-shaped one. Do you want to look or not?
    * [look] "Yes."
@view nell
~ looked_nell = true
A bathroom ceiling, close. A paper lampshade lit from inside, and on the inside of the paper a shadow the size of a hand, opening and shutting.
Her own hand comes up with a pint glass. In the other, for a lid, a folded letter with the council's crest on it.
SOUND: Wings on paper, like someone flicking through a book fast.
A voice from the doorway, small and very awake.
TOBI: Is it Ari?
NELL: Go back to bed.
TOBI: Is it the Ari from my drawing?
NELL: Tobi. Bed.
* "Hello, Tobi."
    ~ spoke_tobi = true
    A silence from the doorway, then feet going fast down a hall.
    NELL: That's the quickest she's gone to bed in her life. Do that again at eight tonight.
* Keep quiet. Watch the moth.
The shadow stops. The glass goes over it. The letter slides across the rim, and the lampshade is empty and just a lampshade.
Nell climbs down off the bath, glass held out in front of her like something that might spill, and gets the window open with her elbow.
SOUND: A window catch. Air. Nothing.
NELL: Did you see that? Tell me you saw that.
* "I saw it."
    NELL: Witness. Great. Somebody finally saw me do something.
    ~ nell_witness = true
* "You were very good with the glass."
    NELL: Nine years in care work. Glass and a letter, that's the whole job.
@state tobi_drawing on
NELL: Right. While you're here. Tobi drew you. For school. A person who helps in our community. I said I'd send it you if you ever turned up.
NELL: So. You turned up.
@text_doc nell tobi_drawing "tobi says she left the face for later"
~ k_tobi_drawing = true
@show_doc tobi_drawing
* "Why no face?"
    NELL: She said she didn't know it yet. She said she'd do it when she met you.
* "It's a good coat."
    NELL: It's a massive coat. She's obsessed with the coat. I don't know where she got the coat from.
* "Tell her thank you."
    NELL: I will. She'll pretend she's not pleased.
if looked_nell:
    She's typing on her phone with one thumb, the pint glass still in the other hand. You're looking where she's looking, so you're looking at her screen.
    * [look] Read the name at the top of her screen.
        -> ch2_nell_screen
    * Look at the ceiling instead.
        ~ b_nell_phone = true
        ~ nell_screen_polite = true
        The lampshade. Empty. Still swinging a little.
        NELL: Thank you for that, by the way. Not reading it.
-> ch2_nell_end

